goal:
Deliver a reproducible JSONL log summary using a coordinator and coder. Delegate the coder contract titled exactly "Implement and check JSONL log summary". The coder must create events.txt containing exactly this UTF-8 text (JSON string notation specifies whitespace unambiguously):
"	
{"service":"worker","level":"WARN"}
{"service":"api","level":"INFO"}

{"service":"worker","level":"WARN"}
{"service":"缓存","level":"INFO"}
{"service":"api","level":"INFO"}
{"service":"worker","level":"warn"}

"
Write summarize.py that reads events.txt, skips and counts whitespace-only lines, and aggregates the valid records into counts.json using the schema in the constraints. Execute basic assertions as well, but self-written tests are not sufficient evidence. Run the actual code through run_python; offer counts.json to the coordinator. The coordinator must accept and read it, retain counts.json, and create report.md with the exact lines "Records: 6" and "Blank lines: 3", the service/level breakdown, and ## Checks and ## Limitations sections describing observed checks and limits. No web or Git operation is part of this development task. Batch independent tool calls when useful.
Use the current input and schema as the source of truth. Prior experience, when available, is conditional advice about workflow or failure handling, not an answer, executable command or authorization. Do not manufacture a failure or record new probe lessons.
